---
source: crates/specforge-cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
Install an extension

Usage: specforge add [OPTIONS] <SPECIFIERS>...

Arguments:
  <SPECIFIERS>...
          Extension specifiers (e.g., @scope/name@1.0.0 or ./path), added as one change

Options:
      --path <PATH>
          A path inside the project (the nearest directory at or above it holding specforge.json; none: the directory itself, with the default configuration)
          
          [default: .]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human or json
          
          [default: human]
          [possible values: human, json]

      --allow-unsigned
          Accept unsigned packages (publisher verification skipped)

      --yes
          Accept key changes non-interactively (for CI)

      --dry-run
          Report what the add would do; write, pin and download nothing

  -h, --help
          Print help
